@page "/"

<PageTitle>ThemeSwitch — Home</PageTitle>

<div class="theme-hero">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow">✦ Application 07</div>
    <h1 class="hero-heading">Light & Dark<br />Theme Switcher</h1>
    <p class="hero-body">
        A Blazor Server app with localStorage-persisted theme switching.
        Your preference is saved across sessions — even after a full page reload.
    </p>
    <div style="margin-top:2rem; display:flex; gap:1rem; justify-content:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <a href="/theme-demo" class="btn-accent">🎨 See Theme Demo</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr)); gap:1.25rem;">
    <div class="card-surface">
        <div class="feature-label">Feature</div>
        <div class="feature-title">💾 Persistent Storage</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">
            Theme preference is saved to <code>localStorage</code> and restored automatically on each page load.
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-surface">
        <div class="feature-label">Feature</div>
        <div class="feature-title">⚡ Instant Toggle</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">
            One button in the top bar switches the entire body class — every component reacts via CSS variables.
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-surface">
        <div class="feature-label">Feature</div>
        <div class="feature-title">🎨 CSS Variables</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">
            All colors are driven by CSS custom properties so switching classes triggers a cascade update with no flicker.
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-surface">
        <div class="feature-label">Feature</div>
        <div class="feature-title">🔗 JS Interop</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">
            <code>IJSRuntime</code> reads and writes localStorage from within C# Blazor component lifecycle.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>